<title>USA: Chase Manhattan expected to issue debt.</title>
<headline>Chase Manhattan expected to issue debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chase Manhattan Corp is expected to tap the corporate bond market with a $250 million debt offering, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to consist of a two-year note and will be underwritten by Chase Securities Inc, dealers said.</p>
<p>Among prior deals, on June 9, Chase Manhattan issued $250 million in 7-1/8 percent 12-year subordinated notes at 68 basis points over U.S. Treasuries. Chase Securities underwrote the deal.</p>
<p>(( -- Nancy Leinfuss, corporate bond unit, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
